WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.760
The SCP Foundation has encountered and contained&nbsp;
some of the most fearsome entities in human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.840
history, and even some from long before us shaved&nbsp;
apes were ever walking across the Earth. They’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:17.360
gotten their hands on ancient gods, humanoid&nbsp;
creatures with deadly powers, and more than one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:22.240
item with the capacity to bring about the end of&nbsp;
the world as we know it. But not everything at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:29.840
SCP Foundation can kill you or would even want to!
Sometimes, an SCP has no agenda other than going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:35.280
about their lives, making friends, or even helping&nbsp;
people. Instead of wanting to eat you for dinner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.560
these entities would rather sit down for a meal&nbsp;
and a chat with you. No apocalyptic ambitions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:47.280
here, just good vibes. Today, we’re taking a&nbsp;
look at some of the friendliest SCPs of all time.&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:54.560
First off is an SCP that’s just as sweet as&nbsp;
it is sad. If you ever encounter SCP-4999,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.040
you probably don’t have long left to live.&nbsp;
That’s not because it’s going to kill you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:05.200
or even hurt you, but because 4999 visits&nbsp;
people who are already at death’s door.&nbsp;

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:11.840
Manifesting as a humanoid figure dressed in dark&nbsp;
clothing, SCP-4999 appears to a person about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:18.000
20 minutes before their death, as long as the&nbsp;
subject is awake and alone. It will then sit down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.400
near their bed, and offer them a cigarette. It&nbsp;
will then light one for itself, and, as it smokes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:29.840
hold the dying person’s hand or place a comforting&nbsp;
hand on their shoulder. It will stay there with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:36.000
them, providing a silent sense of peace, until&nbsp;
they have slipped away. It may not be friendly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.400
in the most traditional sense, but SCP-4999&nbsp;
displays a great deal of kindness and compassion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:48.560
in making sure that no one ever dies alone.
Though some of the friendliest SCPs are serious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.640
others are quite silly.
This is the case for SCP-2991. The entity is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.760
striped, multi-colored scarf capable of changing&nbsp;
lengths. The scarf appears to be sentient,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.720
and behaves in a docile manner, communicating&nbsp;
by forming itself into the shape of letters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:10.480
spelling out words. The scarf enjoys attention and&nbsp;
becomes bored if left in its containment box for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:16.080
too long, and has expressed a desire to play.
When asked if it was “made to be fun,”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:21.680
the scarf responded “yes,” and then wrapped itself&nbsp;
around the interviewer’s hand and went to sleep.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:27.040
It does not seem to have any interests other than&nbsp;
playing and spending time wrapped around people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.160
keeping them warm and cozy. It’s basically&nbsp;
just an ordinary scarf, except it is able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:37.600
move on its own and desires the company of&nbsp;
humans. Sounds pretty darn friendly to us.&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.080
Some SCPs are perfectly nice, friendly&nbsp;
people who have no control over their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.000
own anomalous properties, and would&nbsp;
probably prefer to just live out a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.800
mundane existence free from any unusual activity.
Unfortunately, you don’t always get what you want,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:59.760
and neither does SCP-507. 507 is, for all&nbsp;
intents and purposes, an ordinary human man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:06.160
with one notable exception. Against his will, he&nbsp;
routinely finds himself teleported into alternate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:12.560
dimensions, appearing in them and returning to his&nbsp;
original one seemingly at random. Aside from these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:18.960
odd, stressful occurrences, 507 is a jovial&nbsp;
individual who enjoys meeting other SCPs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:23.840
chatting with researchers at the Foundation about&nbsp;
the paranormal. Aside from his dimension-hopping,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.240
he is no different from any pleasant&nbsp;
stranger you might encounter on the street.&nbsp;

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.120
While some entities, like 507, behave&nbsp;
like a neighbor to the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:40.320
others, like SCP-131, are more like house pets.&nbsp;
SCP-131 refers to a pair of creatures nicknamed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:46.320
the “Eye Pods,” two teardrop-shaped creatures&nbsp;
about one foot high, one orange and one yellow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:51.360
with a single blue eye in the middle of each of&nbsp;
their bodies. Their intelligence has been compared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.960
to common house cats, and they are very curious,&nbsp;
loving to roll around the facility and see what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:02.080
everyone is getting up to. They appreciate&nbsp;
attention and affection and seek more of it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:08.000
from those who they bond to, following them around&nbsp;
like a lost puppy. They may look strange at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:14.160
but their behavior is downright adorable.
And as you may know from some of our other videos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:18.320
when certain deadly anomalies,&nbsp;
like SCP-173, escape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:24.800
they can storm in and save lives. So they’re&nbsp;
not only adorable, they’re adorable heroes!&nbsp;

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.760
Sometimes, an SCP with the best of intentions&nbsp;
can cause harm to Foundation personnel without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:36.720
meaning to. This was the case for SCP-2337, a&nbsp;
male corn crake bird capable of vocalizations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:42.080
loud enough to cause permanent hearing damage.&nbsp;
Though he possesses this ability, he has never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.120
used it to cause deliberate harm while in&nbsp;
Foundation custody. Instead, he simply wants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:52.480
to chat with the personnel, speaking in a language&nbsp;
similar to English. The bird, which responds to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:58.320
the name Dr. Spanko, is very cooperative and&nbsp;
always excited to speak with research staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.440
especially delighted when called by his name.
He may be a bit loud from time to time, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:09.680
who isn’t? He’s not malicious, just enthusiastic.
Sometimes an SCP’s good intentions are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.520
misinterpreted or inadvertently harmful, but&nbsp;
simply as helpful as they were meant to be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:22.480
Enter SCP-662, a small silver hand bell that,&nbsp;
when shaken, summons a short, well-dressed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.080
classic British butler named Mr. Deeds. Mr. Deeds&nbsp;
will address the ringer of the bell by their name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:33.600
and title, and perform tasks for them. He is&nbsp;
extremely polite, and even when given a task&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:40.080
that he does not wish to or is unable to complete,&nbsp;
he declines with the utmost respect. His style&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:45.520
of friendliness may be more formal, but he’s good&nbsp;
company just the same. And we’ve heard he mixes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:53.600
mean - or in this instance, a “nice” - drink, too.
Many of the nicest SCPs to be around are similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:59.120
to pets, but very few were deliberately&nbsp;
intended to live in one’s home as a companion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:06.240
SCP-111 is an exception. 111 refers to a&nbsp;
species of invertebrates resembling snails,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:12.640
also referred to as Dragon Snails. Unlike ordinary&nbsp;
snails, these creatures are warm-blooded, highly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:18.400
intelligent, and capable of breathing fire. Though&nbsp;
they should be handled with care, hatchlings are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:23.040
capable of imprinting on their owners much&nbsp;
like other baby animals, and likely would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:28.720
make a lovely pet for a fireproofed household.
Unfortunately, they are all in Foundation custody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:34.080
so there is no way to find out for yourself.
Some of the previous SCPs in this video are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:42.880
similar to ordinary pets, but SCP-529 actually is&nbsp;
an ordinary pet, with one small anomalous change.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:48.320
SCP-529, or “Josie,” is a small&nbsp;
house cat with grey tabby markings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:54.480
and only half of a body. Don’t get upset! She&nbsp;
is not injured or in any pain. For some reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:59.760
the rear end of her body, from tail to the&nbsp;
bottom of her ribcage, is simply not there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:05.120
The place where the cat’s body ends appears as&nbsp;
pure black to the naked eye, and absorbs light.&nbsp;

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:10.800
The area does not appear to be invisible, but&nbsp;
it is simply not there. In spite of this, Josie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:15.840
experiences no adverse effects, moving around as&nbsp;
if the back half of her body were still there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:20.080
There are no containment procedures in&nbsp;
place for Josie, and she is allowed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:24.880
freely roam the facility, purring, rubbing&nbsp;
up against personnel’s legs for attention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:30.160
playing with balls of string and little mouse&nbsp;
toys, and begging for pieces of cheese as a treat.&nbsp;

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:34.800
Creatures like Josie the half-cat provide a&nbsp;
morale boost to those that encounter them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:40.880
but entities like SCP-5094 can provide material&nbsp;
benefits to the lives of those they meet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:47.360
and help them to make a change for the better.
SCP-5094, or Miss J, is the main character of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:53.040
children’s educational CD-ROM game called&nbsp;
Miss J’s Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse. Miss J,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:57.040
who is unable to leave the computer&nbsp;
program, has only one interest:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:02.960
educating others. She can teach a given student&nbsp;
about essentially any subject, including particle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:07.600
physics and Cubist sculpture. She conducts&nbsp;
her lessons over the course of several days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:12.960
up to 30 hours in length, with breaks for meals&nbsp;
and trips to the bathroom sprinkled throughout.&nbsp;

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.520
Test subjects who studied with Miss J have&nbsp;
described her as the best teacher they have ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:22.960
had, and she helped a D-Class leave the Foundation&nbsp;
and begin a career studying criminal justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:27.440
She even recognized a former student, now&nbsp;
a Junior Researcher at the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:32.320
and expressed delight at seeing how far he&nbsp;
had come since her first lesson with them.&nbsp;

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.800
Many of the friendlier SCPs have a great&nbsp;
deal of knowledge they are eager to share,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:44.560
and one of the most eager out there is SCP-1867,&nbsp;
or Lord Theodore Thomas Blackwood. Lord Blackwood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:49.280
identifies himself as a British explorer and&nbsp;
naturalist as well as a war veteran, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:55.520
is a bit perplexing considering that he is also a&nbsp;
neon sea slug measuring only 4.6 inches in length.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.520 --> 00:09:00.320
In spite of this, he enjoys telling anyone who&nbsp;
will listen, the tales of his past expeditions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:05.600
which he has been able to provide ample proof of.
Lord Blackwood is happy to provide entertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:11.040
and engaging tales of adventure to anyone who&nbsp;
would like to listen to the stories of a sea slug.&nbsp;

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:15.520
If you’re interested in the company of Lord&nbsp;
Blackwood because of a fondness for stories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:21.920
then you’ll also want to hear about SCP-1230.&nbsp;
1230 is a simple unlabeled green hardcover book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:28.160
with nothing strange about it, at first glance.&nbsp;
When it is opened, the phrase “a hero is born”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:33.120
can be seen on the first page the reader looks&nbsp;
at, and the rest of the pages will appear to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:38.640
blank. The true anomalous effects of the book&nbsp;
do not kick in until the reader goes to sleep.&nbsp;

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.040
There, they will find themselves in a&nbsp;
fantastical world as the protagonist of their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:48.880
adventure story. The dream world feels real,&nbsp;
as real as the waking world, and the story is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:54.480
tailored to the interests of the reader. In the&nbsp;
dreams, a bearded man in a green cloak appears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.480 --> 00:10:01.280
known as the Book Keeper, and acting as the&nbsp;
voice of SCP-1230. He is helpful and kind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:05.840
providing guidance to the dreamers and attempting&nbsp;
to ensure that they have a wonderful time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:11.520
in their dream. Just before the dreamer wakes&nbsp;
up, the man bids them a sorrowful farewell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.960
and asks that they “please visit again soon.”&nbsp;

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:19.360
It seems that the book and its keeper want&nbsp;
nothing more than to give readers an incredible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:24.720
experience, and the chance to live out their&nbsp;
wildest dreams as the hero of their own story.&nbsp;

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:30.480
Speaking of objects that help people fulfill&nbsp;
their dreams, SCP-2203 devotes itself to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:36.800
fulfilling romantic dreams in the waking world.&nbsp;
2203 is a standard “Love Tester” machine which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:43.040
upon use, dispenses a card with the name and&nbsp;
address of a person, as well as a bit of advice on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:49.040
how to approach them. This person is intended to&nbsp;
be the soulmate of the subject, and, when subjects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:54.720
approach their chosen person, they find that there&nbsp;
is an immediate spark. Test subjects who sought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.720 --> 00:11:00.160
out their assigned person have found either&nbsp;
a spouse, a lover, or a lifelong best friend.&nbsp;

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:04.640
It refuses to suggest matches to individuals&nbsp;
with a history of domestic violence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:10.080
indicating that its intention is to only make&nbsp;
matches that will be happy, healthy, and safe.&nbsp;

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:15.600
Many of these friendly SCPs display a strong&nbsp;
desire to help others however they can. Few show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:23.360
this desire more strongly than SCP-2295. 2295 is&nbsp;
a patchwork stuffed teddy bear made from synthetic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:28.880
fiber and cotton. When it is near a human who has&nbsp;
experienced major trauma to an organ, the bear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:34.240
becomes active. It will produce scissors, white&nbsp;
thread, and sewing needles or a crochet hook,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:39.520
and create a stuffed version of the ailing organ.
The damaged organ will, somehow, be replaced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:44.240
with this new creation. It sounds as if&nbsp;
this is the start of a horrifying story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:50.000
but it isn’t. The stuffed organ will function&nbsp;
perfectly, defying all known laws of medicine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:55.600
and science. The bear wants to help so badly&nbsp;
that, if there are no useful materials nearby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.600 --> 00:12:01.120
it will use stuffing and fabric from its own body&nbsp;
to construct these organs. When the bear is unable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:06.480
to help a subject, it will do whatever it can to&nbsp;
cheer them up and make them happy, and has even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:12.560
been known to hold the subject and cry if there is&nbsp;
nothing else it can do. Above all, the bear simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:18.160
wants to help heal the hurt and the sick.
Without a doubt, the friendliest SCP that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:24.560
the Foundation has ever encountered is&nbsp;
SCP-999, also known as the Tickle Monster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:30.080
999 is a large mass of orange slime that wants&nbsp;
nothing more than to play, socialize, and make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:35.520
people happy. Its behavior has been compared to&nbsp;
that of a dog, enjoying the company of humans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:40.880
and other creatures. Just touching its slimy&nbsp;
surface is enough to boost a person’s mood, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:46.560
the creature expresses special interest in people&nbsp;
who are unhappy or suffering from emotional pain.&nbsp;

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:52.000
It refuses to eat meat and goes out of its way to&nbsp;
prevent any harm to those around it, even taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:57.760
a bullet for a person to save their life. 999 is&nbsp;
such a delight to be around, that it even managed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:05.120
to make the omnicidal rage of SCP-682 subside,&nbsp;
if only for a moment. Dogs might be considered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:11.680
man’s best friend, but SCP-999 is giving them some&nbsp;
fierce competition for the role. Though, it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:18.320
probably want to be best friends with a dog, too.
And hey, if you want your own SCP-999 to cuddle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:23.120
make sure to check out scpswag.com to pick&nbsp;
up a Tickle Monster plush. It’s the next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:29.120
best thing to having your very own SCP-999 to&nbsp;
cuddle whenever you need a little pick-me-up!&nbsp;

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:35.440
Now go check out “SCP-5031 - Yet Another&nbsp;
Murder Monster” and “SCP-999 and the Most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:41.120
Wholesome SCPs” for more SCPs that’ll warm&nbsp;
your heart and put a smile on your face!

